Subject: [PATCH] fix(diffs): preserve parsed blank-line change positions
 (#1142)

* fix(diffs): preserve parsed blank-line change positions

Parsing a patch could move blank-line changes to different rows,
misaligning highlights and review comments with the source patch.

Limit blank-line sliding to new or edited blocks during active editing.
Keep untouched changes stable and restore parsed positions when editing
ends. Leave similarity-based pairing unchanged.

Fixes #1139

* fix(diffs): keep patch-positioned blank changes in place while editing

Render a git patch whose added or removed blank line sits in the middle
of a run of blank lines, load the files to edit it, then edit somewhere
else in the file. The change highlight jumps to the top of the run on
that first edit even though the blank line was untouched.

The session rebuild re-parses the old and new files, and that parse
reports a blank-run change at the bottom of the run. The lookup for the
previous block only checked that one index, so a block the patch placed
anywhere else in the run was treated as new and slid to the top.

Let the slide callback return a distance instead of a yes/no, and search
for the previous block at every position between the parsed bottom and
the run's top. A match keeps the block where it was, which also covers
blocks the session slid earlier; no match slides to the top as before.
Runs longer than the parse context window still stop at the hunk edge
and keep the bottom-of-run position.
