Subject: [PATCH] fix(diffs): avoid stack overflow when rendering massive diffs
 (#1113)

* fix(diffs): avoid stack overflow when rendering massive diffs

A diff whose largest side exceeds `tokenizeMaxLength` is treated as
massive: highlighting is dropped and the diff renders as plain text. That
path groups rendered lines into one bucket per hunk and appends each
bucket with `push(...lines)`.

A spread passes one argument per line, and engines cap how many arguments
a call can take (V8 near 124k, JavaScriptCore near 639k), so a single hunk
above that cap threw `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` while
appending. Both public entry points reach it: `renderDiff`, used by
`FileDiff`, and `asyncRender`.

Append one entry at a time instead, which has no such ceiling. Batching
the spread was measured and rejected: it is slower than the loop on
JavaScriptCore and reintroduces a hardcoded guess at an engine limit.

Adds a regression test that renders a single-hunk 700k-line diff, sized
above the highest argument limit of the engines the package supports.

